# The collector's wake cost ON A REAL NODE — runco, 2026-09-09
#
# i4i.large spot (x86_64, AL2023, kernel 6.18), 3-node all-spot
# cluster, REAL S3 (us-west-1). Read from the syncer's own log line,
# which this release added for exactly this purpose.
#
#   flint-forge: reclaim examined 17 pack(s) in 17 ms, dropped 0 (0 B)
#
# THE STEADY STATE, which is the one that matters: it walked every
# named pack, found nothing to collect, and returned BEFORE the CAS.
# So 17 ms is the walk and nothing else — ~1 ms/pack.
#
# The COLLECTING case reads higher and must not be quoted as the wake
# cost: 'examined 6 pack(s) in 42 ms, dropped 2' includes an S3 CAS
# round trip and ten unlinks. That is network, not the walk.
#
# Against the models:
#   lima aarch64   ~0.5 ms/pack
#   runco x86_64   ~1.0 ms/pack   (2 vCPU spot node)
#   darwin arm64  ~12.9 ms/pack   (the outlier — macOS forks slowly)
#
# The OBJECT term (~6 us/object) is NOT validated here: the drill
# repositories are tiny. The 1M-object extrapolation remains an
# extrapolation.
